                <pb facs="0452" n="1916" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1916"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AB/12–1351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gifford</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-13T19:00:00+00:00">December 13,
                            1951—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2730. Subject Kashmir. In meeting Dec 12, CRO
                    concurred FonOff view that until elections
                    over in India it will be impossible get any substantial concessions from GOI. Therefore some way must be found bridge gap
                    between Graham’s report and end of January when elections over. Impossible in
                    circumstances avoid SC res which critical of
                    India and which contains recommendations for concrete action.</p>
                <p>UK wld favor res containing recommendations to both parties and asking them
                    consider fully and thereafter report back to SC,
                    perhaps within given time limit. This view of course dependent on whether Graham
                    report lends itself to such treatment; it shld not, for example, be too
                    condemnatory of India.</p>
                <p>Tel along above lines will probably be sent Paris tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Rptd info priority Paris 1266, New Delhi 57, Karachi 50.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gifford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
